  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "wrong_value",
      "components": ["C8"],
      "pins": ["U3.6", "U3.5"],
      "nets": ["VCC", "GND"],
      "observed": "On the NFC_IC sheet, C8 (the bypass capacitor tied between the U3 VCC pin and GND) is drawn with a value of 100p (100 pF).",
      "expected": "The specification's power section lists C8 as one of the 100 nF VCC–GND local bypass capacitors ('C2, C3, C4, C5, C6, C8 — 100 nF each, VCC–GND (local bypass)'). The value is off by three orders of magnitude.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "NFC_IC sheet (nfc_ic.kicad_sch): capacitor labeled 'C8' with value '100p' connected between the VCC arrow (U3 pin 6 VCC) and the GND symbol (U3 pin 5 VSS)."},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "Decoupling / bulk capacitance directly on VCC–GND ... C2, C3, C4, C5, C6, C8 — 100 nF each, VCC–GND (local bypass)."}
      ],
      "impact": "The NT3H2111's VCC pin loses its intended 100 nF high-frequency decoupling; a 100 pF cap is far too small to bypass the IC's supply, so the NFC tag IC is under-decoupled at its pin and may exhibit supply noise or unstable operation that the reference design did not.",
      "confidence": 0.7
    }
  ],
  "summary": "Tracing the three sheets against the spec, the MCU pin assignments, I2C/touch/display netlists, J1 SWD header, and the SSD1306 charge-pump/bias network all match; the one deviation is C8 on the NFC sheet, drawn as 100 pF where the specification defines it as a 100 nF VCC–GND bypass capacitor."
}

